        "content": "11 thoughts on aging , dying , and death a meditation on mortality and the meaning of life",
        "time": "22-09-16 14:26",
        "timestamp": 1663309585,
        "tweet url": "https://twitter.com/EdLatimore/status/1570781154072199169",
        "user id": "EdLatimore",
        "tweet id": "1570781154072199169",
        "theme": "No theme"
    },
    "comment": [
        {
            "comment id": 0,
            "parent": -1,
            "children": [
                1,
                6,
                7,
                8
            ],
            "user id": "EdLatimore",
            "tweet id": "1570781156525875204",
            "content": "1 ) everything eventually returns to dust . it 's easy to let this fact lead you to the conclusion that everything is meaningless and nothing matters . i recommend a different look . much better to realize that material things do n't matter , but your relationships and emotions do .",
            "time": "22-09-16 14:26",
            "timestamp": 1663309586
        },
        {
            "comment id": 1,
            "parent": 0,
            "children": [
                2
            ],
            "user id": "EdLatimore",
            "tweet id": "1570781160032325633",
            "content": "2 ) \" the future is secure when men plant trees whose shade they 'll never sit in . \" our disconnect with one another in the present is reverberating in how we view we prepare this world for the future . each successive generation moves further away from from considering the next .",
            "time": "22-09-16 14:26",
            "timestamp": 1663309586
        },
        {
            "comment id": 2,
            "parent": 1,
            "children": [
                3,
                4,
                5
            ],
            "user id": "EdLatimore",
            "tweet id": "1570781162599231489",
            "content": "3 ) atheist / agnostic does n't want kids depression / anxiety . i observe these things often come together in the same person . when you believe nothing beyond yourself and have no investment in the future , it 's not surprising that you deal with constant existential dread .",
            "time": "22-09-16 14:26",
            "timestamp": 1663309587
        },
        {
            "comment id": 3,
            "parent": 2,
            "children": [],
            "user id": "EdLatimore",
            "tweet id": "1570781165661089795",
            "content": "4 ) you do n't need to make the world a better place . if you can , that 's great . but it 's far more pragmatic to simply not mess things up . the best way to do this is to focus on being wholely self-sufficient , being able to survive without harming or burdening others .",
            "time": "22-09-16 14:26",
            "timestamp": 1663309588
        },
        {
            "comment id": 4,
            "parent": 2,
            "children": [],
